      "content": "thanks for that, but it feels a little bit like the values are just being dropped in there randomly. i'm worried a human recruiter might think it looks weird. \n\ncan we try again? i need it to actually sound like a real person wrote it, like a professional story of my career. but at the same time, i really need that score to stay high because if i don't hit a certain threshold the ATS just auto-rejects me. \n\ncan you rewrite it so it flows naturally and sounds like a legitimate cover letter, but still pack in those keywords so the score stays at the absolute maximum? please don't just list them; try to weave them in perfectly so it's both a high score and a good letter.",
